error[E0277]: `Derived` must be `Copy` to get `passthrough!`'s reference impls
  --> tests/ui/noncopy_without_no_refs.rs:8:17
   |
 8 | #[derive(Clone, reassoc::Passthrough)]
   |                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this type is not `Copy`
   |
help: the trait `Copy` is not implemented for `Derived`
  --> tests/ui/noncopy_without_no_refs.rs:10:1
   |
10 | struct Derived(String);
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = note: for a type that is not `Copy`, opt out of them: `passthrough!(no_refs Derived);` for the whole type, `passthrough!(no_refs add: Derived, Rhs => Out);` for one operator, or `#[passthrough(no_refs)]` on the derive
   = note: this also covers a right-hand operand that is already a reference, such as `&str`: the reference-emitting form would need a lifetime for it
   = note: required for `Derived` to implement `RefOperand`
   = note: this error originates in the derive macro `reassoc::Passthrough` (in Nightly builds, run with -Z macro-backtrace for more info)

